Xilinx Vivado / standard HDL compatibility fixes for NES_MiSTer.
Applied to a copy of the nes_mister submodule by scripts/prepare_rtl.py.

* Signals assigned in always blocks are declared 'logic' instead of 'wire'
  (Quartus accepts procedural assignments to nets; Vivado and the SystemVerilog
  standard do not).
* Combinational 'always begin' blocks without an event control are written as
  'always @* begin' (Quartus infers this, Vivado only warns).
* Files using the savestate register package import it themselves, instead
  of relying on ppu.sv's import in a shared compilation unit.
* VM2413 (VRC7 audio): case statements get 'when others' choices, and arrays
  indexed by an integer subtype use 'low to 'high instead of 'range.

